{"name":"Hannover Hills","hex":"#685d4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hills","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of hill","A region in which there are many hills; a hilly area."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of hill"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hills"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hanover","blocks":[{"text":"Hanover is the capital and largest city of the German state of Lower Saxony. Its population of 535,932 (2021) makes it the 13th-largest city in Germany as well as the fourth-largest in northern Germany after Berlin, Hamburg and Bremen. Hanover's urban area comprises the towns of Garbsen, Langenhagen and Laatzen and has a population of about 791,000 (2018). The Hanover Region has some 1.16 million inhabitants (2019) and is the largest in the Hanover–Braunschweig–Göttingen–Wolfsburg Metropolitan Region, the 17th biggest metropolitan area by GDP in the European Union."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Hannover_Blick_Neues_Rathaus_01.jpg/330px-Hannover_Blick_Neues_Rathaus_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover","wikidata":"Q1715"},{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill","wikidata":"Q54050"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg/500px-Ha